        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "Interior of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre-Dame_Basilica_(Montreal)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Notre-Dame Basilica (Montreal)\">Notre-Dame Basilica</a>, located in the historic district of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Montreal\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Old Montreal\">Old Montreal</a>, in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montreal\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Montreal\">Montreal</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quebec\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Quebec\">Quebec</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Canada\">Canada</a>. The interior of the basilica, built in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gothic_Revival\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Gothic Revival\">Gothic Revival</a> style, is impressive with vivid colors, stars and filled with hundreds of intricate wooden carvings and several religious statues. It was built between 1823 and 1829 after a design of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_O%27Donnell_(architect)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:James O'Donnell (architect)\">James O'Donnell</a> and it has become one of the landmarks of the city.",
